  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nCalculate the **final position** and **velocity** of a projectile launched at 45° with initial speed 30 m/s after 3 seconds.\n\n## Verification of Physics (Expected Values)\n- vx = 30·cos(45°) ≈ 21.2132 m/s; vy₀ = 30·sin(45°) ≈ 21.2132 m/s\n- Position at t=3: x = 21.2132×3 ≈ 63.6396 m; y = 21.2132×3 − ½(9.80665)(9) ≈ 19.5097 m\n- Velocity at t=3: vx = 21.2132 m/s; vy = 21.2132 − 9.80665×3 ≈ −8.20675 m/s\n- Speed = √(21.2132² + 8.20675²) ≈ 22.74 m/s; angle ≈ 21.1° below horizontal\n\n## Screenshot Verification\n1. **Screenshot 1**: Wolfram Alpha with position query `(30*cos(45 degrees)*3, 30*sin(45 degrees)*3 - 9.80665*3^2/2)` — correctly formulated position calculation.\n2. **Screenshots 2–3**: Result shows point coordinates (30cos45°×3, 30sin45°×3 + 3²/2×(−9.80665)) with visual representation labeled **(63.6, 19.5097)** and equation x = 45√2 (≈63.64), y = 19.5097. ✓ Matches the claimed position.\n3. **Screenshots 4–5**: Second query `(30*cos(45 degrees), 30*sin(45 degrees) - 9.80665*3)` for velocity, showing point **(21.2, −8.20675)** and equation x = 15√2 (≈21.213), y = −8.20675. ✓ Matches the claimed velocity components.\n\n## Response Verification\n- Position (63.6396 m, 19.5097 m) — confirmed by screenshots ✓\n- Velocity (21.2132 m/s, −8.20675 m/s) — confirmed by screenshots (15√2 = 21.2132) ✓\n- Speed ≈ 22.74 m/s and direction ≈ 21.1° below horizontal — not shown in screenshots, but per guidelines, content in the response not shown on the screenshot can be believed, and these derived values are physically correct.\n\nBoth required components (position AND velocity) were computed correctly using Wolfram Alpha, and the response accurately reports the results.\n\n## Verdict\n**SUCCESS**",
